From 4db1348ab1eb51e16872a433fc83443c7a1219bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:58:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] Eden (Doris): fuller performance report; CPU profiler
 on for now

The 10-second performance report now also says, per game frame:
- how many draws, compute dispatches, render passes and submits there were,
  and how many new pipelines had to be built;
- how long the GPU emulation thread waited for a free presentation frame and
  for GPU fences, and how long the Vulkan worker waited for shader builds;
- how much GPU time the frame took in all, and how much of it went to frame
  generation and to scaling the image to the screen (GPU timestamps);
- how often the GPU emulation thread and the Vulkan worker sat on prime,
  middle or little cores.

The CPU profiler is on by default while the speed-up work needs data.
